  mapped  annotation enable-modsecurity (ingress-nginx's modsecurity.conf): SecRuleEngine DetectionOnly: mode: Detect
  mapped  targetRefs: IngressRoute blog: the Ingress's hosts and paths
Ingress files/cloud: WAFPolicy files/cloud (Detect), WAFRuleSet files/cloud-modsecurity
  mapped  annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 1: Include /etc/nginx/owasp-modsecurity-crs/nginx-modsecurity.conf: the built-in OWASP CRS v4
  TODO    annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 2: not migrated: Include /etc/nginx/owasp-modsecurity-crs/plugins/nextcloud-rule-exclusions-before.conf: Inkwall can't read files from the ingress-nginx pod; put the rules in a WAFRuleSet
  check   annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 4: SecRequestBodyLimit 13107200: body.maxBytes: 10485760, the most Inkwall inspects; bodies between the two limits are now over the limit (body.onOversize)
  TODO    annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 5: not migrated: SecRequestBodyNoFilesLimit 131072: no equivalent in Inkwall
  check   annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 6: SecRequestBodyLimitAction ProcessPartial: body.onOversize: Allow; ModSecurity inspected the first part of an oversize body, Inkwall forwards it uninspected
  check   annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 7: not migrated: SecAuditEngine RelevantOnly: ModSecurity's own logs; the engine logs verdicts itself (protection is unchanged)
  check   annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 8: not migrated: SecAuditLog /dev/stdout: ModSecurity's own logs; the engine logs verdicts itself (protection is unchanged)
  mapped  annotation modsecurity-snippet, line 9: kept in the WAFRuleSet: SecRuleRemoveById 941000-942999
